<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

	<PropertyGroup>
		<TargetFrameworks>net8.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
		<GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
		<PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
		<Title>TestFramework.Core</Title>
		<Authors>DeadMoon0</Authors>
		<Product>TestFramework</Product>
		<PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
		<PackageTags>Test;UnitTest;IntegrationTest;Framework;Fluent;Timeline</PackageTags>
		<PackageIcon>Icon.png</PackageIcon>
		<Description>The core package of the TestFramework ecosystem for building integration-style and end-to-end test workflows. Provides the timeline engine for steps, events, variables, artifacts, retries, timeouts, and assertions, and serves as the foundation for extension packages like Azure, LocalIO, and Simple.</Description>
		<Version>0.2.0</Version>
		<PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/DeadMoon0/TestFramework-Core</PackageProjectUrl>
		<RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/DeadMoon0/TestFramework-Core.git</RepositoryUrl>
		<RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
		<Copyright>Copyright (c) DeadMoon0 2026</Copyright>
		<PackageReleaseNotes>Debugger protocol v2 (breaking for debugger consumers): events now travel in a versioned envelope framed as length-prefixed UTF-8 instead of UTF-16, and the signal types are public so a consumer no longer needs InternalsVisibleTo.
Attaching is cheaper and no longer latched: a listening UI is detected per run with a directory probe instead of a connect timeout, so a UI started midway through a suite is picked up without setting TESTFRAMEWORK_DEBUG_PIPE.
Runs can be recorded to an NDJSON journal under %APPDATA%\TestFramework\Debug, gated on that directory existing, so a completed run stays inspectable after the test host exits. Nothing is written when the directory is absent.
A failed step now reports why: exception chain, stack trace, attempt number, and the FriendlyMessage/RecoverySteps/AvailableOptions of framework exceptions.
Runs report a real test identity (fully qualified name, framework, source location, project file) instead of a bare method name, and can be stopped cooperatively so the timeline unwinds through its Cleanup stage rather than being killed.
Fixes: artifact version captures and lifecycle changes now reach debuggers; variable change detection no longer drops updates whose values differ only past the 120-character display cut-off.</PackageReleaseNotes>
	</PropertyGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
	  <None Include="..\Modules\TestFramework-Common\Assets\Icon.png">
	    <Pack>True</Pack>
	    <PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
	  </None>
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<AssemblyAttribute Include="System.Runtime.CompilerServices.InternalsVisibleTo">
			<_Parameter1>TestFramework.Config.Tests</_Parameter1>
		</AssemblyAttribute>
		<AssemblyAttribute Include="System.Runtime.CompilerServices.InternalsVisibleTo">
			<_Parameter1>TestFramework.Core.Tests</_Parameter1>
		</AssemblyAttribute>
		<AssemblyAttribute Include="System.Runtime.CompilerServices.InternalsVisibleTo">
			<_Parameter1>TestFramework.Simple.Tests</_Parameter1>
		</AssemblyAttribute>
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<PackageReference Include="Newtonsoft.Json" Version="13.0.4" />
		<PackageReference Include="xunit.abstractions" Version="2.0.3" />
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
	  <None Include="README.md">
	    <Pack>True</Pack>
	    <PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
	  </None>
	</ItemGroup>

</Project>
